  "limitations": [
    "Real annotation correctness is a proxy outcome, not real onboarding success.",
    "Observed-participant replay is conditional on historical assignment and does not estimate a causal gain or performance across unobserved workers.",
    "Only official partitions 1, 6 and 11 are used by default; a label-independent hashed task sample is selected.",
    "Tasks spanning temporal cutoffs are purged. No task or outcome crosses the retained split boundaries.",
    "Source truth is used only to derive correctness labels; task answers and truth are never inference features.",
    "Location, certification, verification, capacity and availability are absent; neutral values are used, not claimed as real.",
    "Content scores are constant in this proxy setup. Workload is constant, so the load-rule baseline reduces to an ID tie-break.",
    "Wilson intervals assume independent tasks; repeated workers and tasksets may make them optimistic.",
    "Scores are ranking values, not calibrated success probabilities."
  ]
